# The root Cargo.lock is tracked (reproducible extension builds + cargo audit in
# CI). The guest crates are build-time wasm tooling — their lockfiles stay out,
# with one deliberate exception.
/guests/boa/Cargo.lock
/guests/rustpython/Cargo.lock
# wizen/ is that exception. It runs the LAST step of the TypeScript guest build,
# and the fixture is claimed to be byte-for-byte reproducible on a pinned
# toolchain. An unlocked Wizer (and the Wasmtime it pulls in) can resolve
# differently on another machine or on another day, which would make the claim
# unearned. Tracked so it is earned — and so `cargo audit` has something to read.
